From: Павел Левицкий <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: rx1950: mark zImage entry with the green LED

The HaRET log proves the loader has completed its CRC check and jumped into
zImage, but the normal board-level LED marker is too late to distinguish a
decompressor failure from a later machine initialisation failure.  RX1950 is
the only target of this kernel configuration, so light its active-low green
LED at the first executable instruction after the legacy zImage header.

---
 arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S b/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S
--- a/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S
@@ -222,0 +223,12 @@ start:
+		/*
+		 * RX1950 boot probe: GPIOA6 is the active-low green LED.
+		 * HaRET has disabled the MMU before branching here, so use the
+		 * S3C24xx physical GPIO register block directly.  This must remain
+		 * position-independent because zImage may be relocated by HaRET.
+		 */
+		ldr	r0, =0x56000000
+		ldr	r1, [r0]
+		bic	r1, r1, #0x3000
+		orr	r1, r1, #0x1000
+		str	r1, [r0]
+		ldr	r1, [r0, #4]
+		bic	r1, r1, #0x40
+		str	r1, [r0, #4]
ARM_BE8(	setend	be		) @ go BE8 if compiled for BE8
